  "notes": "⛔ **The arrangement block is the model.** The research is unusually direct about this: the per-beat internals belong to his co-producers, and what is unambiguous across the catalog is the posse-cut grammar — hook-first, sequential guest verses of 8–16 bars each separated by the hook, a full drum drop-out before each new voice, and a layer-additive final hook. So `arrangement.structures` is authored with four verse slots rather than two, `sectionBars.verse` is a weighted choice of 8 or 16, `dropOutBeats.prob` is 0.95 over four beats, and the intro is short because the tag is the intro. Around it, anthemic settings: `velocityTiers` lifted to the top of the range, orchestral `crash`/`impact`/`riser` lanes on the downbeat for the 8-bar boundaries, triplet hats with big 32nd/32nd-triplet fills, `dualLayerProb` 0.45 for the snare roll before each guest entry, and the widest melody register in this batch (60–96) for horns, strings and choirs. ⚠ `medium`, and the reason is in the research: the arrangement is high-confidence and everything else on this page is house-anthem inference from co-produced records, not from a Khaled interview about programming. The drum, 808 and melody numbers are the inferred ones.",
